description:
Adjudicate legacy data-item gold keyed on source field names rather than canonical concepts.

Measured: 308 of 436 annotations match no current rule under any alias because they record source fields such as `id`, `name`, `token`, `location`, `status`, `key`, `uid`, and `uuid`.

For each row:

- preserve the observed source token and evidence;
- assign a canonical concept leaf when the evidence supports one;
- otherwise move it to `needs_adjudication` or reject it with rationale;
- do not keep a source-token-only row accepted merely by calling it no-concept.

An explicitly unclassified concept may be accepted only if the canonical ontology deliberately defines that scored leaf; it may not be invented as a migration escape hatch.

Repository-level canonical entities consolidate repeated evidence only after concept and entity grouping are adjudicated. The pass records every legacy row outcome so none disappear from readiness accounting.

This human-reviewed annotation work gates baseline readiness.
